      "writtenOn": "2024-01-11T04:09:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Suggest not making this function asynchronous but instead just running the code inline. If you don\u0027t run the code inline, the caller cannot know when the operation is complete, and if the caller (in this case, ConnectivityService) sends async callbacks to *its* callers, then those callbacks can be called before this operation is complete. This makes it difficult for the users of those callbacks to figure out what is going on.\n\nGiven that this code is tightly coupled to ConnectivityService (it\u0027s a global singleton in the system server process, owned only by CS itself), then we can just have CS pass in its own handler. I think this is what we do in other classes such as KeepaliveTracker.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 428,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 428,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "0c1057abec9b05ccce971d0d933a1255775bb561",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
